{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs32 Summary\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Platform and data engineering leader with 6+ years of building cloud data platforms and a PhD in Information Engineering (434 citations, h-index 10). At Cardo AI I lead the platform/infrastructure and data engineering teams behind a multi-tenant structured-finance SaaS: multi-account AWS in the EU and US, 10 EKS clusters, an Apache Iceberg lakehouse served by Trino and Spark, and the GitOps, identity and security layers around them, including the infrastructure controls for its SOC 2 Type 2 audit. I contribute upstream to Trino and Airflow, was nominated as a Trino Champion, and spoke at Trino Summit 2024.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs32 Skills\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Data:} Trino, Apache Spark (Spark Connect), Apache Iceberg, Delta Lake, Apache Airflow, Kafka, Debezium, PostgreSQL / Aurora, Snowflake, PyIceberg, DuckDB, Databricks.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Platform:} AWS (multi-account, EKS, Glue, S3, IAM Identity Center), Kubernetes, Karpenter, KEDA, Terraform, ArgoCD, Helm, HashiCorp Vault, Keycloak, Kyverno, GitHub Actions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b FinOps:} Savings Plans, Cost and Usage Reports, OpenCost, spot capacity.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Observability and security:} Grafana LGTM stack, Prometheus, AWS Security Hub, GuardDuty, WAF, Prowler.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Languages:} Python, SQL, Bash, Java, C++, R.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs32 Experience\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Feb 2025 \u8211- present \u9830? Head of Platform & Data Engineering @ Cardo AI\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Lead the platform/infrastructure and data engineering teams ({\b 5 engineers}) behind Cardo AI\u8217's multi-tenant structured-finance SaaS: {\b 21 AWS accounts in the EU and US} (landing zone extended to the EU in 2025), {\b 10 EKS clusters and 17 tenants}, fully defined as code (Terraform, ArgoCD GitOps, a 38-chart Helm library) so any environment can be rebuilt from Git. Hands-on throughout: 1,790 merged PRs across 54 repositories and 730+ code reviews since 2022.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Re-platformed the data synchronization of Cardo AI\u8217's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cardoai.com/solutions/by-product/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
structured-finance platform
}}}
 onto an {\b Apache Iceberg lakehouse} (S3, AWS Glue, Spark Connect, Trino, Airflow) with incremental silver/gold pipelines, retiring the legacy pipeline after bit-for-bit parity tests. Led the migration from Delta Lake to Iceberg (12,000+ Iceberg tables) and moved 1,754 Glue databases into 16 per-tenant AWS accounts with zero downtime, using a parallel, dry-run-first migration tool.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Tuned the core Spark sync from plan-level analysis: memory and disk spill from 130 GB + 42 GB to {\b zero}, shuffle-write time from 253 s to 29 s, a 1.17-billion-row history rescan replaced by a 9-million-row partition read, and Iceberg files compacted from 2,988 \u215? 10.6 MB to ~83 \u215? 383 MB.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Retired the materialized reporting tables in favour of query-time derivation in Trino, so queries that used to run out of memory now complete. Benchmarked 413 production query shapes, traced the remaining regressions to a 19\u215? cardinality underestimate and rewrote the views to run at or below the tables\u8217' cost. Migrated 1,026 stored client SQL definitions across 13 tenants and 4 services with zero differences on 597k parity-checked rows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Built an internal {\b Trino platform Helm chart} that generates catalogs, Vault credentials and access control from a declarative tenant model, replacing ~2,800 lines of hand-written YAML per deployment. Validated the migration by replaying 14M+ access decisions, then ran zero-downtime blue/green Trino upgrades.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Designed {\b multi-tenant workload isolation for Trino}: client tags route interactive, batch and AI-agent (MCP) queries into weighted per-tenant resource groups with server-side time limits and an 85% memory gate, sized from 28 days of query-log data, so a single tenant\u8217's burst no longer starves the cluster. Cut compute cost with Karpenter spot pools on the cheapest local-NVMe instance type (~20\u8211-25% lower hourly price), spill to disk, fault-tolerant spooling on S3 Express One Zone and working KEDA autoscaling.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Designed {\b tenants-as-code} in Terraform: one YAML catalog generates databases, Keycloak realms, Trino users, TLS certificates, CDN frontends and VPN routes for every tenant. Shipped it as a zero-downtime refactor (584 state moves, no resource replaced) guarded by plan-time checks and a {\f1 terraform test} CI suite.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Delivered the cloud-infrastructure controls for Cardo AI\u8217's {\b SOC 2 Type 2} audit (Security, Jun 2025 \u8211- Jan 2026), passed with no exceptions: IAM Identity Center SSO in place of IAM users, EKS Pod Identity, multi-realm Keycloak with Google and Microsoft federation, AWS Config, Security Hub, GuardDuty, Prowler and WAF, plus point-in-time restore for the lakehouse (Iceberg time travel) and per-tenant PostgreSQL.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Set the platform team\u8217's engineering standards: design docs, runbooks and architecture pages in the company documentation, stacked pull requests with zero-diff Terraform plans and Helm render diffs as acceptance criteria, and staged dev \u8594? staging \u8594? production rollouts.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Run FinOps for the AWS estate: Savings Plans and instance-mix analysis from the Pricing and Savings Plans APIs, Cost and Usage Reports and Prometheus usage, with an integer-programming optimizer. Plans run at 100% utilization and save 42% of on-demand-equivalent compute spend, with a further ~$10\u8211-12k/year identified.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Aug 2023 \u8211- Jan 2025 \u9830? Data Engineering Tech Lead @ Cardo AI\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Designed Cardo AI\u8217's {\b multi-account AWS landing zone} on the Well-Architected Framework (shared-VPC networking, infrastructure management, shared and per-customer workloads, artifact repository, log archive, security tooling) and rolled it out in the US in 2024.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Built centralized observability for EKS clusters across accounts on the {\b Grafana LGTM stack} (Loki, Grafana, Tempo, Mimir) with storage in the log-archive account, plus immutable, cost-efficient CloudWatch log collection to S3 (subscription filters, Kinesis Firehose) and cross-account monitoring.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Implemented automated {\b change data capture with schema evolution for ~800 RDS PostgreSQL tables} into Delta Lake (Strimzi Kafka, Debezium, Schema Registry/Avro, Spark Connect streaming, Airflow on EKS), packaged as an internal library with Prometheus alerts, Grafana dashboards, a self-healing connector DAG and source-vs-lake reconciliation; later open-sourced as kafka2delta.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Moved {\b Trino workers onto spot instances} by adding graceful worker shutdown to the official Trino Helm chart (upstream), so workers finish their running tasks before a spot interruption takes the node and fault-tolerant execution on an S3 exchange retries the rest. Added spill to disk, Alluxio cache on NVMe nodes, ARM64 workers and off-hours downscaling.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Built the data-science platform on EKS with Terraform and ArgoCD: Kubeflow (deployKF), MLflow, shared GPU nodes and Karpenter node pools for workload separation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Automated per-team Airflow environments with Terraform modules and ArgoCD, with Kyverno-enforced workload segregation and OpenCost cost allocation; added a shared Spark Connect server and an OpenMetadata data catalog.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Replaced AWS Client VPN with self-hosted zero-trust access (NetBird, then Firezone) across clusters and accounts, and set up multi-account Terraform CI/CD with GitHub Actions, AWS CodeBuild and self-hosted runners on EKS.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 Sep 2022 \u8211- Jul 2023 \u9830? Senior Data Engineer @ Cardo AI\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Built Cardo AI\u8217's first data engineering platform on EKS as primary author: Trino (OAuth2, TLS, Vault), Airflow, Spark Operator, Superset, Kafka and JupyterHub, delivered with Argo CD.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Rebuilt the data platform on AWS in 2023 with a reusable Terraform module library (EKS, Karpenter, ArgoCD, Vault, Airflow, Trino), GitOps delivery and dev/prod pipelines with approval gates, then retired the legacy cluster.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Built on-demand Spark processing on Kubernetes orchestrated by Airflow, using a custom Spark build with a Glue-enabled Hive metastore and Delta Lake; released as internal Airflow providers (Spark-on-Kubernetes operator, IRSA-based Vault secrets backend) and later as the open-source {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/sdaberdaku/apache-airflow-providers-pysparkonk8s"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
